      "body_md": "Palm Beach Bots is both a retailer and a product designer, so its database records need to distinguish PBB/Palm Power products from resold Repeat, FingerTech and Just 'Cuz parts. The PBB 2822 family is a useful example: the catalog carries several KV/shaft combinations as upgraded stock-form-factor weapon motors, while kits such as Plastic Poison and Dead Shaft Delight integrate those motors with BLHeli_S ESCs and Repeat/FingerTech drive hardware. Palm Power batteries are purpose-sized for ants, and the B6 Neo is the higher-feature charger option. Resold manufacturer products should normally resolve to their manufacturer record rather than being duplicated as a new PBB component."
